  "comment": "MiniMax H3 head replacement by inpainting. The source clip is masked (a hand-painted static region, or SAM3 video tracking), cropped to the subject, and only the masked region is denoised: NKDAVLatent encodes the crop into a joint audio+video latent and puts the mask on it as a noise_mask, so the unmasked pixels and the WHOLE soundtrack are held. Holding the audio is what makes the new head lip-sync -- the model sees the original speech while it paints the face. Identity comes from the reference pictures (nodes 120-128, <Picture N>), exactly as in reference mode. The result is pasted back into the untouched frames by MVEx_SubjectUncrop.\n\nTHREE MASK BRANCHES, and the MCP prunes the two not chosen: 152/166/167/153 is the painted static mask (conformed to the footage and repeated to its frame count, so a single PNG authored in the browser is legal input); 154/155/156/157 is SAM3 video tracking on the lane itself; 168/169/170/171 is a mask SEQUENCE already tracked elsewhere (the hosted SAM3 service, or any tool that can write a white-on-black clip), which is how a lane with no SAM3 checkpoint still gets a tracked mask. As shipped, node 159 reads the SAM3 branch.\n\nNeeds, beyond the ordinary H3 lane: Nekodificador/ComfyUI-NKD-Basic-Tools (MIT) for NKDAVLatent + NKDMaskOps, drozbay/MaskVidExperiments (GPL-3.0) for the subject crop and uncrop, and -- for the SAM3 branch only -- comfy-core's native SAM3 video nodes plus checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors. See packages/gpu-rentals provisioning.",
